SGTL tutorial patch for HypoDD 2.1b by Felix Waldhauser (https://github.com/fwaldhauser/HypoDD,
tag V2.1b, commit fb40407fb768cbdc23a11e27bc841f5d4a98abb7). install/components/tools.sh applies it.

1. include/hypoDD.inc: MAXDATA 3000000 -> 15000000, the most differential times (observations)
   hypoDD can hold. The lab uses this size for large catalogs. The arrays then need more than
   2 GB of address space, so tools.sh compiles with -mcmodel=large (memory is used only as needed).
2. src/hypoDD/Makefile: remove an LDFLAGS line that points to the library folder of an old macOS
   compiler and breaks linking on Linux. (tools.sh also gives LDFLAGS on the make command line,
   which replaces the same line in src/ph2dt and src/ncsn2pha.)

